1.48.m:
Brahmā said:
Unsolicited alms are declared to be commendable;
better than that is the gleaning livelihood, which is auspicious above all livelihoods,

1.49.m:
and relate in full the practice for the other castes.
Brahmā said:
From good conduct one gains long life, from good conduct one gains happiness;

1.50.m:
The brāhmaṇa said:
"O Lord, let our mind abide in you in every way;
except for you, O Lord of all worlds, let nothing ever please [it]."

The Blessed Lord said:
"Mūka is always devoted to his parents; she is an auspicious, faithful wife;
Tulādhāra speaks the truth and is impartial toward all people;
